  "notes": [
    "Valid entries must decode successfully; byte_exact entries must also re-encode to the exact file bytes. The marked exceptions are the whitespace-padded boundary fixture and the JSON-escaped fixture, which decode to canonical values but are deliberately not canonical bytes.",
    "Invalid entries must be rejected with exactly the listed error category.",
    "Duplicate JSON keys are always shape errors, in every position: a plain data field, the correlation id, an internally tagged type tag, or a nested reason. Non-Rust decoders must reject duplicate keys rather than accepting the last value; JSON-test last-value-wins semantics are non-conforming for this contract.",
    "Protocol errors have closed payload-free reasons. The codec permits correlation presence for any reason; the owner omits it for Hello or undecodable input and echoes it only for decoded correlated requests.",
    "The future-range Hello (2..=3) is valid JSON for this schema and must decode; negotiation with this codec then rejects it because the codec supports only version 1.",
    "The oversize payload is a valid Hello padded with insignificant whitespace to 16385 bytes, so the payload cap is its only defect; a decoder without the cap would accept it.",
    "All structs use JSON objects and all enum tags use strings. Arrays and numeric enum indices are shape errors, including in nested fields."
  ],
